{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"The value of the series is the limit, as $~n\\to\\infty\\,$, of the sequence of partial sums.\n\nThat is, $\\displaystyle S=\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}S_n$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\displaystyle\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}{{S}_{n}}=\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\frac{n^2+1}{n+1}=\\infty$\n\nHence, $S$ diverges.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"The $n\\text{th}$ partial sum of the series $S$ is given by\n\n$\\displaystyle{{S}_{n}}=~\\frac{n^2+1}{n+1}$.\n\n**Determine $S$.**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$S=1$","correct":false},{"content":"$S=2$","correct":false},{"content":"$S=\\frac{1}{2}$","correct":false},{"content":"$S$ diverges.","correct":true}],"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"onePerLine":true,"randomize":false},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
